      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've been having similar Issues converting a friend's model. At first, I thought it was the lack of sphere collision but since then that's been added and it helped a little. To add to the main post it seems as if the interpolation in between bones is really stiff and allows for very minimal movement.\nIn this example, I rotate the head as if you were looking down and the bones just do not want to flow down along the collider whatsoever unless I set gravity to either pretty high with no pull or max out the gravity. Also noting even with max Elasticity in DB the bones still flow down the colliders instead of shooting outwards presumably towards the rest pose.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-01T23:43:46.236Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "PB colliders seem to push bones out of the way and back to the default resting pose instead of sitting still with the collider it interacts with. And it feels more like... a ball...? that stays in one place and just rotates rather than actually moving/stretching like DB",
